# Compiled bytecode is transport debris, not evidence.
#
# operating-environment/.gitignore already said this, and said it had been
# removed by hand twice. It then happened a third time — in tools/ and tests/,
# which are siblings one level ABOVE the directory that ignore covers. The rule
# was right and its scope was too narrow to reach where the next occurrence was.
# Placing it here covers control-plane/** including operating-environment/**.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
